    "Condition : 1 - The London Borough of Hounslow as the Local Planning Authority hereby certify that on 22 July 2026, the existing use of the premises as a House in Multiple Occupation (HMO) (Use Class C4) was lawful within the meaning of Section 191 of the Town and Country Planning Act 1990 for the following reason:\r\n\r\nThe existing use would comply with the requirements of Schedule 2, Part 3, Class L of the Town and Country Planning (General Permitted Development) (England) Order 2015 (as amended) and it has been demonstrated, on the balance of probability, that this use commenced prior to the Article 4 Direction coming into effect.\r\n"
